# Internationalization Rules

Keep backend locale behavior predictable.

## Requirements
- `en` is the baseline locale.
- Locale resolution may consider user preference, tenant default, and `Accept-Language` headers.
- All user-facing API messages must use translation keys resolved through the i18n layer; no hard-coded user-facing strings outside `src/locales/`.
- Error `code` values must stay stable and language-neutral; localized text lives in `src/locales/`.
- Backend-generated messages must use translation keys or localized message helpers.
- Stored user-entered clinical, legal, and mortuary notes must remain unchanged.
- Date, time, and number formatting helpers must be locale-aware at the API boundary.
- Keep copy concise with appropriate clinical/operational terminology.
